msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-xbee.rst:30
#: 8c23b22346274f849c0be9a3b88e3738
msgid "Click on the diagram at the top of this page to see the individual wire connections that must be made between the autopilot and Xbee module. Note that in the diagram above only 4 wires are connected (GND, 5V, Transmit, Receiver). The CTS and RTS (Ready-to-send) pins are left unconnected because although connecting them should improve the data rate during the creation of this wiki page we were unable to successfully connect. With the CTS and RTS pins disconnected the BRD_SER1_RTSCTS (if using Telem1) or BRD_SER2_RTSCTS (if using Telem2) should be set to zero (after making the change the autopilot will need to be restarted)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-xbee.rst:44
#: 76f6ad979edd4baf9bb5836e79b4065c
msgid "The `X-CTU <https://www.digi.com/products/xbee-rf-solutions/xctu-software/xctu>`__ application can be used to configure the XBee modules."
msgstr ""

